        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Rethrow mid-turn precheck signal through harness",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- rethrow mid-turn precheck signals before persisting assistant failure messages\n- also preserve the signal through public harness entrypoint catch blocks\n- keep ordinary agent loop failures on the existing failure-message path\n\n## Why\n\nThe mid-turn tool-result precheck throws `MidTurnPrecheckSignal` so the embedded runner can compact and retry before the next model call. `CoreAgentHarness.executeTurn()` was catching every `runAgentLoop()` error and converting it into an assistant error message, and the public harness entrypoints also normalize caught errors. The signal needs to pass through both layers so the outer attempt runner can observe it.\n\n## Validation\n\n- patched and restarted the local OpenClaw gateway with the same harness changes\n- confirmed compare shows one changed file: `packages/agent-core/src/harness/agent-harness.ts`\n- inspected OpenClaw 2026.5.28 session JSONL evidence showing mid-turn precheck errors persisted as assistant failures before compaction entries",
